# Security headers for the static build.
#
# This file format is read by Cloudflare Pages and Netlify. It is copied into
# the build output as-is and ignored by hosts that do not understand it, so it
# is harmless if you deploy somewhere else. Firebase Hosting does NOT read it —
# use firebase.json, which carries the same list.
#
# Whatever ends up serving this, the headers below need to be present. Check
# with: curl -sI https://apply.iecse-manipal.com | sort
#
# Notes on the CSP, because a wrong one breaks the page silently:
#   script-src has no 'unsafe-inline'. The Vite build emits no inline scripts,
#     verified against dist/index.html, so it does not need it and should not
#     have it.
#   style-src does need 'unsafe-inline'. React sets element style attributes in
#     five places, which CSP counts as inline styles.
#   connect-src must include the Supabase project the API runs on. Without it
#     every submission is blocked by the browser before it leaves.
#   img-src needs data: for the canvas fallback, which draws to a data URL.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'

# Hashed filenames, so these can be cached hard.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The entry point must never be cached, or a deploy does not reach anyone.
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
